6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stein</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Santos</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nagatomi</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayashi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Minnery</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Xavier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cool (TRPM8) and hot (TRPV1) receptors in the bladder and male genital tract</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>2004</year><volume>172</volume><fpage>1175</fpage><lpage>1178</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15311065</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Segen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kemmler</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Increased levels of Met-enkephalin-like immunoreactivity in the spinal cord CSF of rats with adrenal medullary transplants</article-title><source>Brain Res</source><year>1989</year><volume>502</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2819448</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spaziante</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Merola</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Colao</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Beta-endorphin concentrations both in plasma and in cerebrospinal fluid in response to acute painful stimuli</article-title><source>J Neurosurg Sci</source><year>1990</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>99</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2092099</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><p